MERGE MESSAGE BODY:
#### Summary
The Invite Guest modal's "Add to channels" section was rendering with hard-coded or dimmed text colors that did not respect the active theme. On dark themes the typed input text and the parenthetical channel name in the suggestion dropdown were nearly unreadable against the themed background.

This PR makes the section follow the active theme:

- Adds `color: var(--center-channel-color)` to the shared `InviteView__sectionTitle` so the "Add to channels" heading uses themed text.
- Adds `color: var(--center-channel-color)` to the channel picker control and to `.channels-input__input-container`. The previous attempt only fixed the outer control and the inner input but missed the input container that `react-select` uses to drive the inherited input color, so the typed text was still rendering in the default `rgb(51, 51, 51)`.
- Replaces the `opacity: 0.5` overlays on `.channel-name` (and its `(` / `)` pseudo-elements) with `color: rgba(var(--center-channel-color-rgb), 0.75)` so the parenthetical channel name stays readable on dark themes while still being visually de-emphasised.

